{"name":"Coronation Blue","hex":"#59529c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"coronation","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An act of investing with a crown; a crowning.\n\n An act or the ceremony of formally investing a sovereign or the sovereign's consort with a crown and other insignia of royalty, on or shortly after their accession to the sovereignty.","An act or the ceremony of formally investing a sovereign or the sovereign's consort with a crown and other insignia of royalty, on or shortly after their accession to the sovereignty."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coronation"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Coronation","blocks":[{"text":"A coronation ceremony marks the formal investiture of a monarch with regal power using a crown. In addition to the crowning, this ceremony may include the presentation of other items of regalia, and other rituals such as the taking of special vows by the new monarch, the investing and presentation of regalia to them, and acts of homage by the new monarch's subjects. In certain Christian denominations, such as Lutheranism and Anglicanism, coronation is a religious rite. As such, Western-style coronations have often included anointing the monarch with holy oil, or chrism as it is often called; the anointing ritual's religious significance follows examples found in the Bible. The monarch's consort may also be crowned, either simultaneously with the monarch or as a separate event."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Charles-vii-courronement-_Panth%C3%A9on_III.jpg/330px-Charles-vii-courronement-_Panth%C3%A9on_III.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coronation"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Jacob_Axelsson_Lindblom_kr%C3%B6ner_Karl_XIV_Johan.jpg/500px-Jacob_Axelsson_Lindblom_kr%C3%B6ner_Karl_XIV_Johan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Jacob_Axelsson_Lindblom_kr%C3%B6ner_Karl_XIV_Johan.jpg/1280px-Jacob_Axelsson_Lindblom_kr%C3%B6ner_Karl_XIV_Johan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Jacob_Axelsson_Lindblom_kr%C3%B6ner_Karl_XIV_Johan.jpg/500px-Jacob_Axelsson_Lindblom_kr%C3%B6ner_Karl_XIV_Johan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The coronation of Charles XIV John of Sweden, by Evangelical-Lutheran archbishop Jacob Axelsson Lindblom (1818); detail of the painting by Per Krafft the Younger","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJacob_Axelsson_Lindblom_kr%C3%B6ner_Karl_XIV_Johan.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Martorana_RogerII2008.jpg/500px-Martorana_RogerII2008.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Martorana_RogerII2008.jpg/1280px-Martorana_RogerII2008.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Martorana_RogerII2008.jpg/500px-Martorana_RogerII2008.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Roger II of Sicily receiving his crown directly from Jesus Christ, mosaic from Martorana, Palermo","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMartorana_RogerII2008.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/An_ancient_coronation.jpg/500px-An_ancient_coronation.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/An_ancient_coronation.jpg/500px-An_ancient_coronation.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An ancient coronation from the Indian subcontinent","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAn_ancient_coronation.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Demetre_I_%28Matskhvarishi%29.jpg/500px-Demetre_I_%28Matskhvarishi%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Demetre_I_%28Matskhvarishi%29.jpg/500px-Demetre_I_%28Matskhvarishi%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The coronation of King Demetrius I of Georgia by the angels, 12th century","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File